# Optional settings for ops/scrape.sh, ops/catalog.sh and ops/primers.sh. To use them, copy this to
# ~/.config/mooligan-data/env and run
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/mooligan-data/env
# because the keys are secrets. The scripts warn when the mode is looser.
#
# One KEY=VALUE per line. No `source`, no $variables, no trailing comments. Quotes around a value are
# stripped. A variable that is already set in the environment wins over this file, even when it is
# set to empty.
#
# GitHub Actions runs and publishes the data. Nothing here is needed to run the scripts on a laptop:
# by default they upload nothing and read the live files from data.mooligan.com.

# The keys are only for reading the R2 bucket directly (SYNC=r2) or publishing from this machine
# (PUBLISH=1), which is the exception. Cloudflare dashboard > R2 > Manage API tokens: an Account API
# token with Object Read & Write on the mtg-meta-data bucket only. The Account ID is on the R2 overview
# page. Cloudflare shows the secret once; if it is lost, make a new token.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=mtg-meta-data

# 1 uploads to R2 (needs the keys, and for the scrape SYNC=r2). Anything else uploads nothing.
# PUBLISH=1

# Scrape: where the previous snapshots and state come from.
#   auto   r2 when the keys are set, else https (the default)
#   r2     the bucket
#   https  the live files at DATA_URL, no keys needed
#   none   an empty start, which begins the 30-day backfill of mtgo.com and MTGTop8
# SYNC=auto
# DATA_URL=https://data.mooligan.com

# Scrape: a small, fast run for development (modern only, 3 days of history, 10 minutes of requests, no
# EDHREC, locator, premier schedule or movers). Each of its settings can still be set by hand. Never published.
# QUICK=1
# FORMATS=modern,standard,pioneer,legacy,pauper,vintage,premodern,duel_commander
# HISTORY_DAYS=30
# mtgo.com and MTGTop8 are asked one page at a time, this many seconds apart (never under 5), for at most
# SCRAPE_MINUTES a run.
# SCRAPE_DELAY=10
# SCRAPE_MINUTES=90
# 1 starts the scrape from nothing, ignoring the downloaded snapshots and scrape state (local files only).
# FRESH=1
# An empty value switches the locator off.
# LOCATOR_PLACES=Singapore

# Catalog: recompute every image vector, or limit the cards for a quick run.
# FULL_REBUILD=1
# MTG_LIMIT=200

# Scrape: Claude polishes the commander guides' summaries as one Message Batch (about $0.0125 a guide).
# ops/scrape.sh only does so on a run that publishes, unless GUIDE_POLISH=1. The key is a secret.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=
# GUIDE_POLISH=1

# Primers: ops/primers.sh writes the archetype primers with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (above), spending at most BUDGET
# dollars, and with PUBLISH=1 publishes them with the API Worker's admin token. The token is a secret.
# Its FORMATS takes only standard, pioneer, modern, legacy, pauper and vintage.
# PRIMERS_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# BUDGET=5
